#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:20
#: fac5ff77479f4e03b5da429db8efc65b
msgid "In addition, analog temperature monitors and DroneCAN based sensors can be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:22
#: 79465fee89e6405eb6d1ff003622dfd9
msgid "ArduPilot already has numerous possible sources for temperature reports: ESCs, Smart Batteries, Motor EFI and these independent sensors can be used to replace those devices temperature reports which already exist in ArduPilot. They can also just be logged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:25
#: 695cf90f78514cd292cc5837bfb4b559
msgid "I2C Sensor Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:27
#: 1498feaf3ff44bafa970f212acc7177a
msgid "Attach the sensor to one of the autopilot's I2C ports using SDA and SCL pins. Then set (examples shown for the first sensor):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:29
#: d81062e3e7c449c886b43081d9a321ef
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_TYPE<TEMP1_TYPE>` = 0:Disabled, 1:TSYS01, 2:MCP9600, 3:MAX31865, 4: TSYS03, 7: MLX90614"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:30
#: 8fef23a6fc7c4fa5b557f56637cec8db
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_BUS<TEMP1_BUS>` = the I2C port on which the sensor is attached (0-3)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:31
#: 6609881855f14ef09603dd691b13c48a
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_ADDR<TEMP1_ADDR>` = the sensor's I2C address (0-127)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:32
#: 7ffccb94bbc54cb088bfe790c140461d
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_SRC<TEMP1_SRC>` = the temperature reporting device type that should have its temperature report replaced with this sensor's. (Optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:33
#: 163aa4a9538f46308de63511b23e41b4
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_SRC_ID<TEMP1_SRC_ID>` = identifies the individual device, of the above type, that should have its report replaced. (Optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:35
#: 71b5fca289994514bbba223497fbdcf3
msgid "Each I2C device on any single bus must have a unique address. If more than one of the same type of I2C temperature sensor is used, ensure each is configured with a unique address. Some breakout boards include jumpers for this purpose. Refer to the product datasheet for specific instructions regarding I2C address configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:37
#: 53ea1485c8a34dbfa548d7304fa95680
msgid "The MAX31865 is an SPI device, which uses the same parameters and basic configuration procedure as I2C sensors but must be connected to an SPI port rather than an I2C port. Some autopilots do not expose an external SPI port, in which case the MAX31865 cannot be easily used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:39
#: f02faa8a44064688b8f5b09fbb913abe
msgid "The MLX90614 sensor is an infrared thermometer for non-contact temperature measurements. Its I2C address is 90 so :ref:`TEMP1_ADDR<TEMP1_ADDR>` = 90 for this type of sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:42
#: e90ef7df2a9748f5858ddd8c514b2d8d
msgid "Analog Sensor Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:44
#: 20f5a2c73fc4430389fb3d023857e378
msgid "Attach the sensor to an analog input pin (an unused rssi input, analog airspeed input, battery voltage input, or current monitor input pin, for example). The pin number can be determined from the autopilot's wiki page. Use care not to exceed the pin's rated voltage (typically 3.3 volts) with the sensor output. Then set (examples shown for the first sensor):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:46
#: 5f6cc1979a9c4d8db43d2cef0c830791
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_TYPE<TEMP1_TYPE>` = 5 : Analog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:47
#: 8952340ba5494308b49ae3708187359b
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_PIN<TEMP1_PIN>` = the analog pin number (for example: 2:Pixhawk/Pixracer/Navio2/Pixhawk2_PM1, 5:Navigator, 13:Pixhawk2_PM2/CubeOrange_PM2, 14:CubeOrange, 16:Durandal, 100:PX4-v1, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:49
#: 65f384f35f494dcaa4d985ad99404e6e
msgid "The output voltage vs temperature curve of the sensor can be adjusted to match its characteristic via a polynomial (up to 4th order). Fit the curve via the product datasheet, a spreadsheet application, MATLAB, Python/numpy, etc:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:51
#: 75487b23998449b1b456790f5439e9f1
msgid "``deg = a0 + a1*voltage + a2*voltage^2 + a3*voltage^3 + a4*voltage^4``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:53
#: b32b1b099559432591f6f2837c49c265
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_A0<TEMP1_A0>` = a0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:54
#: dc095c71fcfe42bc988e0e2f28beeb72
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_A1<TEMP1_A1>` = a1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:55
#: aa785f6f5f604f73899ffc94b78baf3b
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_A2<TEMP1_A2>` = a2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:56
#: 3f7a3bf73def4c79bec98dd3490f65ca
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_A3<TEMP1_A3>` = a3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:57
#: 7e855c408def47f59d8011dcf29519db
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_A4<TEMP1_A4>` = a4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:60
#: 84052272d99d434480535038d95cf271
msgid "DroneCAN Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:62
#: 254c312feb6b4cb789540f8f2027f97b
msgid "Make sure the CAN port is setup. (example below for first CAN port using first driver):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:64
#: d94f46805e8d4200b5fb5d8b5b0a7849
msgid ":ref:`CAN_P1_DRIVER<CAN_P1_DRIVER>` = 1 (First driver)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:65
#: 9ccc0617d48843758f5e2f0669c3846a
msgid ":ref:`CAN_D1_PROTOCOL<CAN_D1_PROTOCOL>` = 1 (DroneCAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:67
#: d4e974f1c9b64a28834a3f431305a7bf
msgid "Then set (examples shown for first sensor):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:69
#: f9b75215d26c47fbaf50ae45b6841a66
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_TYPE<TEMP1_TYPE>` = 6 (DroneCAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:72
#: 45807ba0f9bc455f9dbb916d46ee0e79
msgid "Logging/OSD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:74
#: 4a5f4b0f7bc0418c9440ee902d99c652
msgid "Several peripherals have the possibility of reporting temperature if their hardware permits: ESCs, EFIs, Smart Batteries, etc. However, if their hardware does not include a temperature sensor, it's possible to redirect a discrete temperature sensor's report to be included with another device's report. We will use the first temperature sensor below as an example. This also allows the OSD ESC or Airspeed (if DroneCAN) temperature panel to be used for OSD display of the temperature sensor if an ESC temperature is not being reported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:76
#: 1696ee7500ea499fb16ad2b521a06b99
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_SRC<TEMP1_SRC>` will designate which device's temperature report will be replaced by this temperature sensor's data. ie: if set to 1, then an ESC's report of temperature(usually null due to lack of hardware capability)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:77
#: 66b4ad4872fe4c3f8cc9192794e449ca
msgid ":ref:`TEMP1_SRC_ID<TEMP1_SRC_ID>` replaces a specific instance of a system component's temperature report with this temp sensor's. ie: if set to 4, with the above param set to 1, the fourth instance of an ESC (ie 4th motor/servo output with a motor/throttle function) will have its temperature report replaced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-temperature-sensor.rst:79
#: f6d1da1ea62b44ff9fcf6513973ac074
msgid ":ref:`TEMP_LOG<TEMP_LOG>` = 0: No logging, 1: Log temperature reports from all temperature sensors, including those also being reported in other device reports, 2: Only those with ``TEMPx_SRC`` set to NONE, eg. not being logged elsewhere."
msgstr ""
